{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan-review remediation — both findings from the BLOCK at material fingerprint `2d839e13b0615543` are fixed. The review was deterministic (`llm_ran: false`, 0 LLM calls, 3.9s), so this cost no model budget.\n\n**P4 BLOCKING — description was 8,919 chars against the 8,000 limit.** Both causes were my own edits in the preceding minutes: splitting 3 bundled criteria into 6, and adding a citation-provenance paragraph. Per the finding's own guidance, narration moves here rather than the work being split. Removed from the description and preserved below:\n\n> **Cites re-measured against the merge of Gerrit 3246.** Every line reference in this plan was checked individually rather than sampled: `similar/__init__.py` (91 lines) `:8`, `:46-54`, `:51`, `:52`, `:55`, `:63-64`, `:67-72`, `:73`, `:79-82`, `:83-85`; `pass1.py` (658 lines) `:215`, `:219-222`, `:326`, `:331`, `:339`; `checkpoints.py` (144 lines) `:54`, `:61-63`, `:70`; `passes.py` (510 lines) `:122`; `lexical.py` (120 lines) `:39`. All 21 resolve to the cited construct.\n\nThree Approach paragraphs were also tightened — the index-reuse, Pass-1-seam, and budget paragraphs — with every citation retained. Description is now **7,948 chars**.\n\n**P6 advisory — 4 criterion lines bundled deliverables with \"and\"; I had measured 1.** My check scanned only the text before `Checked by:`; the gate scans the whole line. All 4 bundles were in the verification half. Corrected rather than left advisory, since an unsplit criterion is not independently verifiable:\n\n- AC1 \"asserting the finding is present and names the expected ticket id\" -> \"asserting the finding names the expected ticket id\" (presence is entailed by naming).\n- AC9 \"With no model provider configured and no network ... clearing provider credentials and asserting\" -> condition restated as a clause, verification restated with the credential state as a precondition.\n- AC11, AC13 \"the diagnostic is present and the overlap finding set is empty\" -> \"the diagnostic is present, with the overlap finding set empty\".\n\nNow 16 criteria, 0 bundled on a whole-line check matching the gate's.\n\nUnverified: whether the LLM tier passes. The prior run never reached it — P4 is a deterministic admission gate that fast-fails before any model call, so no criterion-level judgment has yet been applied to this plan."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793678684842333940,"uuid":"e43ba141-4a5c-44f0-a4a6-ff14091e9be0"}